## commentaire 6874161554 (texte)
Confirmed on current `main`.

In `pkg/image/verifiers/ivpol/cosign/opts.go#L93`, air-gapped key/cert verification with `insecureIgnoreTlog: true` skips Sigstore infrastructure, leaving `opts.TrustedMaterial` nil. 

When `ctlog.tsaCertChain` is provided:
- Line 180 sets `opts.UseSignedTimestamps = true`.
- line 181 guards `opts.TrustedMaterial` construction with `if opts.TrustedMaterial != nil`. Because it is nil, the TSA authority is never wrapped into `opts.TrustedMaterial`.

When `cosign.VerifyNewBundle` later delegates to `sigstore-go`, calling `trustedMaterial.TimestampingAuthorities()` panics with a nil pointer dereference.

Regarding severity: at admission time with `validationActions: [Deny]`, evaluation errors fail-closed and deny the request, so unauthorized images are not admitted; however, signed RFC 3161 timestamps cannot be verified in air-gapped / private-TSA key attestor setups.

Confirmed reproducible bug on `main`. @gigi206 please go ahead and open your PR with the fix and unit tests.




